              "response": {
                "status": "success",
                "text": "Changelog\n=========\n\n3.1.0 (2026-08-19)\n------------------\n\n- Added ``Pool.drain(timeout=...)`` to close idle connections before shutdown.\n- ``Pool.stats()`` now reports ``waiting`` and ``in_use`` separately.\n- Fixed a race in ``Pool.acquire()`` when the pool was resized during a wait\n  (#412).\n- Documentation: new page on running tidepool under uvloop.\n\n3.0.2 (2026-06-30)\n------------------\n\n- Fixed a leak of one connection per failed health check (#398).\n- Wheels for musllinux aarch64.\n\n3.0.1 (2026-05-21)\n------------------\n\n- Fixed ``ImportError`` on Python 3.13 when the optional ``tidepool[otel]``\n  extra was not installed (#381).\n\n3.0.0 (2026-05-04)\n------------------\n\n- Added support for Python 3.13. Wheels are published for CPython 3.9 to 3.13.\n- Dropped support for Python 3.8.\n- Breaking: ``Pool.acquire()`` is now an async context manager only. The old\n  ``await pool.acquire()`` form raises ``TypeError`` with a hint.\n- Breaking: renamed ``max_idle`` to ``max_idle_s``.\n- New ``on_connect`` hook.\n\n2.9.0 (2026-01-12)\n------------------\n\n- Added experimental free-threaded build checks. Python 3.13 is not yet\n  supported; see #350.\n- ``Pool.close()`` waits for in-flight releases.\n\n2.8.1 (2025-11-03)\n------------------\n\n- Fixed type hints for ``Pool.__aenter__``.\n\n2.8.0 (2025-10-02)\n------------------\n\n- Added ``Pool.resize()``.\n- Python 3.12 support."
              }
            }
          }
        ],
